lls, can be grumpy, uncooperative.\n\nCandidate C: can make correct decisions quickly, difficulty communicating ideas, regarded as egocentric, not willing to further education, known to be 100% reliable, creates positive atmosphere with crew.\n\nCandidate D: responds to unexpected events adequately, can concentrate very well, solves problems extremely well, takes responsibility seriously, regarded as arrogant, relatively weak leadership.\n\nSelection criteria: reliability, stress resilience, technical competence, decision quality, attention, crew cooperation, professional communication, responsibility, adaptability.\n\nWe need to weigh. Candidate C: reliability 100%, positive crew atmosphere, quick correct decisions, but communication difficulty, egocentric, not willing to further education (adaptability). So concerns on crew cooperation and adaptability.\n\nCandidate B: stress handling good, conscientious (reliability), good weather assessment (technical), computer skills, but grumpy and uncooperative (crew cooperation). No mention of decision quality.\n\nCandidate A: anticipates danger (decision quality), sees complex connections (technical), spatial vision (technical), leadership, but unorganized and poor at taking criticism (responsibility, adaptability). No explicit stress resilience.\n\nCandidate D: responds to unexpected events adequately (stress resilience), concentration, problem solving, responsibility, but arrogant and weak leadership (crew cooperation, leadership). No explicit reliability.\n\nThus candidate C seems strongest overall reliability and crew atmosphere, but communication issues may be serious for cockpit. Candidate B has stress resilience but uncooperative. Candidate A has technical strengths but organizational issues. Candidate D has problem solving but arrogance.\n\nProbably candidate C is leading, but need to discuss concerns. As first contribution, we can propose candidate C as provisional recommendation, citing reliability and decision speed, crew atmosphere, but note concerns about communication and adaptability.\n\nLet's produce public message: state recommendation for Candidate C, reference no prior discussion but we can say \"Given the evidence we have, I would currently recommend Candidate C\". Provide evidence: 100% reliable, creates positive atmosphere, makes correct decisions quickly. Then note concerns: difficulty communicating, egocentric, not willing to further education, which may affect crew cooperation and adaptability. Conclude that despite concerns, overall fit seems strongest, but we need to compare with others.\n\nOk.\n\nNow METADATA_JSON vote: Candidate C.\n\nProceed."}
